//! Tests ported from Python: umap/tests/test_umap_metrics.py (dense parts)
//! and umap/tests/test_umap_grads.py.
//!
//! The fixed input arrays replicate the pytest fixtures of
//! umap/tests/conftest.py (`SEED = 189212`; `spatial_data` = randn(10, 20)
//! stacked with two all-zero rows, `binary_data` = a random boolean matrix
//! stacked with two all-zero rows), cast to float32. The reference matrices
//! below were generated by umap-learn 0.5.12: the installed numba metrics
//! (umap.distances.named_distances) evaluated on those same float32 arrays
//! (the Python tests cross-check these values against sklearn's
//! `pairwise_distances`, whose non-finite corner cases it patches to the
//! same 0.0/1.0 the metric functions themselves produce).
//!
//! Deviations from the Python tests:
//! - The gradient finite-difference checks use eps = 1e-3 (Python: 1e-6)
//!   and 16 samples (Python: 100) because the metrics compute in f32 and
//!   the data sets are embedded constants; tolerances are loosened
//!   accordingly.

